From 1ffa7650e337861757e801835e0be0bdb3910c49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kris Williams <115474+kriswill@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:41:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] devenv-shell: kitty graphics passthrough for the
 interactive shell
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Programs inside `devenv shell` could not draw images (cachix/devenv#3130):
the child's output is fed to a libghostty virtual terminal and the real
terminal is repainted from it, so kitty graphics APC sequences never left
the VT, the capability query (`a=q`) was never answered, and `CSI 14 t`
plus a zero-pixel PTY left `kitten icat` reporting "does not support
reporting screen sizes in pixels". fastfetch, yazi and icat all fell back
to text.

Fix it from the VT side rather than forwarding raw bytes around it:

* kitty_images.rs: enable kitty graphics in the VT (storage limit, local
  transfer mediums, a PNG decoder on the `png` crate) so it stores images,
  resolves placements and answers the child itself. After every rendered
  frame `ImageSync` mirrors the VT's placements onto the real terminal:
  images are transmitted once per (id, generation) under a private id
  range, placements are made at explicit cursor positions on the rows the
  renderer drew, clipped to the content area so nothing covers the status
  line, deleted when the VT drops them, and removed on exit. All commands
  carry `q=2`, so the real terminal's replies never reach stdin.
* The VT's `ESC _ G … ESC \` replies pass the deny-by-default pty-write
  filter; the child's own commands still never reach the real terminal.
* cell_size.rs: probe the real terminal's cell size with `CSI 16 t` at
  startup and after resizes, intercepting the reply on stdin. It gives the
  PTY pixel dimensions (so `TIOCGWINSZ` works), the VT its cell geometry
  (so placements resolve to grid cells) and answers `CSI 14 t` for the
  child's area, which excludes the status row. Until the terminal answers,
  `CSI 14 t` is forwarded as before.

The PNG decoder is thread-local in libghostty-rs and must be installed on
the VT thread before the terminal is created. Cargo.lock only gains png
and fdeflate; Cargo.nix regenerated accordingly.

Tests: unit tests for the clipping math, command encoding, probe
interception and a libghostty-backed round trip; pty session tests for
the `a=q` answer, a mirrored PNG placement and the `CSI 14 t` reply.
